If you have driver software for a Sony CDU-541 then you could do this:

Open the box (its pretty simple.)  On the back of the CD-ROM are some jumpers
(probably a cable connecting the SCSI ID select button to the jumper area.
One is labeled PARITY.  It actually controls what the controller board of the
CD-ROM thinks it is.  Removing this will cause the drive to think it is a 
SONY CDU-541. And you are off and running.

PLEASE NOTE:  Doing this would uh probably violate whatever sort of field 
circus agreements you have with your provider and/or your warranty.  Ie. if it
breaks put the jumper back on before having it serviced or sending it in for
repairs to DEC.

