A few weeks ago I reported a problem with a Wangdat 2600 after upgrading a
VS4000 model 60 to a model 90 at VMS 5.5-2.  The symptom is the DAT drive goes
off line (and into mount verification) after about 30 seconds of writing data
from a local disk via BACKUP/IMAGE.  The error log contains the following entry
for the PKA0: device:

	ERROR TYPE          0706        SCSI BUS PHASE ERROR
                                        PHASE CHANGE TIMEOUT DURING DATA OUT

The problem was fixed after applying CSCPAT #1074 V1.1 which is a new MKDRIVER. 
This patch fixes a different problem on a TK50 (on SCSI) but has the same error
type in the error log entry.  The problem may affect other SCSI tape devices
as well.  Hope this information will save others some grief. 


