In article <1993Feb23.180940.1@ssrl01.slac.stanford.edu> winston@ssrl01.slac.stanford.edu (Alan Winston) writes:
>Folks --
>
>I'm having a problem with DECnet logins on my VAX 8800, running VMS A5.5.
>
>We appear to be limited to 16 simultaneous interactive DECnet logins (RT
>terminals).  The 17th and subsequent login attempts fail with a 
>
>%SYSTEM-F-REJECT, connect to network object requested. 
>

  The problem is that the sysgen parameter RJOBLIM is still at the
  default of 16.  RJOBLIM defines the maximum number of remote
  terminals at any one time.  It's a dynamic parameter, so you can up 
  it without rebooting (use WRITE ACTIVE to have it take effect after
  using SET).  Use WRITE CURRENT in SYSGEN to save it for the next 
  reboot.


--
