>Paul,
>	"binary" FTP transfers is a bit of a sticky point unless you have a
>TCP/IP product that supports the STRU VMS instruction which transfers the VMS
>file structure as well. "Binary" mode only really works for fixed length
>records, and only if the fixed lenght is 512 bytes are you able to use the file
>right away.
>
>	But don't despair! What you should do is to backup your file into a VMS
>Saveset:
>
>	$ BACKUP TEST.BINARY TEST.BCK/SAVE
>
>Next you transfer this saveset in BINARY mode, and on arrival at the other end,
>you use the DECUS program to set the record length back to the 32256 bytes used
>by backup to disk. Finally, you simply unfold your saveset:
>
>	$ BACKUP TEST.BCK/SAVE []
>
>and you're done! In this way, you can transfer any number of files in any of
>RMS's smvrgesbord of formats. ("smorgasbord" in case you don't have an 8-bit
>news-reader..._
>
