What is DecDtm? Very good question.  It stands for Digatal's Distributed
Transaction Manager.  The currently supported calls are documented in
the Version 5.x system service manuals.

The reason I say that it is a good question, the sarcasm has trouble coming
through the keyboard, is because in many ways its a lie.  Dec purports to 
have a truly distributed transaction manager supporting 2 phase commits
across multiple process' and multiple nodes on a network.  And, if you
buy ACMS, or DecIntact, or some other dec product you will have some of
that support.  Everything works fine if your doing all your work on a single
process. However, if you want to do it yourself, e.g. two process'
using RMS Journalling being part of the same transaction, its not there.

Even though all the documentation suggests that you can do this!!!! 

Lucky for me, I have access to the VMS source on CDROM,  I currently work
for a large dec customer.  I found undocumented system service calls
to allow for true distributed transaction management/processing.

IT WORKS!   Why don't they support it?  Or at least stop making believe
it exists when it doesn't.


Hope this helps,  sorry for the diatribe but it's been a very frustrating
couple of months getting through all this.

Alan Sanders
