In article <1993Feb18.093622.28417@ulrik.uio.no>, toreh@bootes.sds.no (Tore Haraldsen) writes:
>Is it possible to re-use the companion TK50 expansion box,
>for instance by hooking it onto the SCSI bus of a VS3100-30?

It misbehaves and may cause problems.  When I hooked one up to a VS3100-38 with
an RZ23, RZ25 and TZ30, I found that the SCSI bus would reset every time I tried
to remove the tape.  Also found that removing the tape was a challenge, as the
door interlock would trigger within one second of opening the door, thus jamming
the tape inside.  The trick was to use two hands; open the door and pull the
cartridge out real quick.

There are two part numbers that I am aware of;

	TK50Z-F*
	TK50Z-G*
	* is country (i.e. 3 for Australia, A for America)

The F one is not "true" SCSI and is for use with the VS2000.
The G one is "true" SCSI, and works fine on my VS4000/VLC that I bought.

>If it is not possible to hook it up as-is, are there parts available
>to convert the TK50 expansion cabinet to SCSI use?

I have *heard* that the F can be upgraded to a G.  I have also heard two
conflicting stories as to what the upgrade contains.  One source says it's
just removing the built-in bus terminator by cutting PCB links, another source
says it also involves a ROM upgrade.

If all else fails, contact Digital.

