This ought to go on the FAQ lists (I have answered this question privately
at least a dozen times over the past year).

To turn VAXstation xxxx with RD-yy HD and zz MB of RAM into something useful,
do the following:

	Throw away (or give away or whatever) your RD-yy small disks

	Make sure your zz MB RAM is 6 MB or more (OK for you).

	Buy licenses for EWS (ELN Window Server) software from DEC
	It is VERY cheap and requires no extra hardware.

This runs a VAX/ELN kernal with DECwindows on the VAXstation xxxx, turning
it into a perfectly good X-terminal.  xxxx include 2000, 3030, 3038, 4030
(VLC), 8000, IIGPX and many more.

Caveat: I think you need a VMS or Ultrix box to boot the kernal (I don't know
if you can actually put it on a small disk - check with DEC). You might use
your "broken" VAXstation II as an "ELN server" (minimal VMS and DECnet boot
service for the EWS machines).

Cheers


