Yes, I totally agree with you. They need to ship compilers that get the most
out of the machine, it's a terrible waste not to. But I'll give them the
benefit of the doubt and give them some more time to get it faster.

I also take issue with the dec philosphy of having the default always be full
optimization, and then not doing a lot of optimizations because they are too
time consuming. There should be a 'final' mode of optimization for production
code that attempts to produce the fastest code possible with few compromises
for compilation speed. This mode would have to be explicitly requested. I
don't give a damn if it takes half an hour to compile some code if it runs
in 6 hours instead of 8 and I'm going to run it 100 times!


