In article <1993Feb18.093622.28417@ulrik.uio.no> toreh@bootes.sds.no (Tore Haraldsen) writes:
>Our old VS2000 is to be pensioned off as an X terminal.
>
>Is it possible to re-use the companion TK50 expansion box,
>for instance by hooking it onto the SCSI bus of a VS3100-30?

Not directly, no. There is a slightly different SCSI bus on the TK50Z-FA
(I think that's the model used on the VS2000).

>If it is not possible to hook it up as-is, are there parts available
>to convert the TK50 expansion cabinet to SCSI use?

There exists a TZK50 controller board that goes inside the TK50Z box
which goes between the VAXstation 3100 (or other SCSI) and the TK50 itself.

Open up the TK50Z box and see if that controller is in there. If you
do have a TZK50, then you should be able to run a cable directly to 
that board. If not, then you might want to look for one. If you can't 
find one and need a TK50Z for your VS3100, then I believe the model number
is a TK50Z-GA


Chris


