>I recently obtained a third party SCSI drive that I want to
>use with my DECStation 5000/125 running Ultrix 4.2a.  I can
>partition and mount it okay, but it immediately starts currupting
>files.  fsck always find problems with the file system.  This is
>the second drive it's happened with, so I'm pretty sure it's not
>the drive itself (Micropolis 1908).
