I did something similar.  I have a VRT19 19" colour on an HX card
with a VRM17 17" monochrome on the baseboard graphics controller.
It sounds like you are missing a line from your kernel config.  Here
are the gory details...

> How did you start the Xws server?
> 
> Is there a reason why both cards would do their powerup screen test ritual,
> but /usr/etc/userf -R reports only two fb devices, fb0: which I assume is the
> on-the-motherboard graphics adapter and fb:, which I assume is one of the
> PMAG-AA cards.

Each turbochannel card should do their self tests.  The fb0: and fb:
you speak of are refering to the same graphics controller.  Each
controller properly configured will give you an fbN: and and fb: line.

Firstoff, For this to work at all, the controllers you want to use
together must be supported by the same X server, in the case of the
baseboard controller, Xws.  Other things (PXG and variants and the PX
under ultrix 4.2) need other servers Xtm2d and like.

There are several things you need to do.

If you want to use the baseboard controller and a turbochannel
controller under Ultrix 4.3, add the -mg flag to the boot command.
Something like
>>> setenv boot "3/rz2/vmunix -a -mg"

In the kernel config file, add lines like this for the number of
controllers you have (including baseboard).
device          fb0        at ibus?     vector fbint
device          fb1        at ibus?     vector fbint

Booting the new kernel should show the frame buffers in the device
configuration section.  My startup shows this;
Turbo->                 fb0 at ibus0
                        fb: Module type PMAGB-BA 1280X1024
baseboard->             fb1 at ibus3
                        fb: Module type PMAG-DV 1024X768

Nothing special needs to be done to Xws startup to see the multiple
controllers.  Because I have placed my screens in the wrong order,
my ttys file ends like this,
:0 "/usr/bin/login -P /usr/bin/Xprompter -C /usr/bin/dxsession -e" none
on secure window="/usr/bin/Xws bc -edge_left0 1 -edge_right1 0"

If you are using Mwm, you should set the multiscreen option in your
Mwm config file to have one Mwm process control all screens.

