You are very close to the answer.  To get the 5400 to autoboot the 
bootmode environment flag must be set to 'a'.  Like this:

>>setenv bootmode a

Good luck,  you may still have problems after a crash since the
boot process will halt and leave the system in single user mode
if there is a problem with disks that are not unmounted properly.

john


