I could say RTFM, but it isn't really friendly :-).

The MIT server CANNOT run on a PX or PXG display; you'll have to run Digital's
server; your favorite R5 applications should run fine with it.  This limitation
is quite clear in the MIT documentation for the R5 release, which will only
run on CX, MX, or HX (in dumb frame buffer mode).

That the kernel is crashing is not good and should be fixed, and the MIT distribution
really should report better if you try to run a server on hardware it doesn't support.
Please enter a bug report both to Digital and to MIT.
