>source of our problems) the root and /var filesystem to this disk and
>mountet the /usr filesystem from the DS5000.

You should rebuild your kernel to support the 5000/125.  You should start
from scratch, so use /etc/doconfig with no arguments and let it build
a new kernel config file.  It would be a good idea to use the genvmunix
kernel before running /etc/doconfig; do something like this:

    # mv /vmunix /vmunix.old
    # cp /genvmunix /vmunix
    # reboot

    # /etc/doconfig
    (answer all the questions)

    # cp /sys/MIPS/SYSTEM-NAME-GOES-HERE/vmunix /vmunix
    # reboot


