At one point I had a c program that was an interactive vt100 terminal
tester. You compile the program on your local host, attach your vt100
or other vt100 emulating device to the host, start the program, and
watch the fireworks.

It would do queries of the terminal to see what response it gave, send
command strings which caused various displays, and ask whether or not
the display was appropriate.

This was a great tool for finding gotchas. It did resolve lots of
is-it-the-terminal or is-it-the-software kinds of issues.

Does anybody know where this may be archived? How about a version for
later terminals in the same series?

Thanks.


