Definitly yes, but you'll need one KDA50-controller for this.
The KDA50 may connect up to 4 RAxx-disks to the system. KDA50 are
not supported on the BA23-box but since your power on the 5V-line does
not exceed 36A, it should do. On the BA123 it will work and is supported.

>
>lso, does anyone know whether it is possible to boot a Micro VAXZ II
>over ethernet (this would save a lot of installation problems).
>
Yes, it may boot over ethernet. On the >>> -level, just type 
>>>b xq
and of it goes. Btw. there's no chance of setting an automated boot-device. 
So any coldstart will result in the boot-attempts DUA0, DUA1... and at last
XQA0.
Hope that helps.

