In article <1993Feb12.110317.98@dallas.sil.org> titus@dallas.sil.org writes:
>  How do I save my printer options (queue, print style,
>etc.) for a DECterm window?  I have tried setting everything.....

Only the information on the first pull down menu will be saved.  That's where
you select print destination, print mode, etc.  You MUST supply a file name.
If you are not printing to a DEC brand printer then you should also select
Print National Characters Only, non-DEC printers don't know how to handle some
of the escape sequences that are generated.  While there is no way to save the
queue name, you can limit the choices of queues to only the one you want.
The logical names DECW$PRINTER_FORMAT_xxx, where xxx is the print format from
the next level pull down menu, can be used to limit the choices.  The way I've
made it work is:

DEFINE/GROUP DECW$PRINTER_FORMAT_DEFAULT LASER1

SET QUEUE/DEFAULT=(FORM=whatever) LASER1

Now, unless you go to the second level pull down menu and change the print
format, all you have to choose from is the queue LASER1 and any printscreens
submit to that queue with the form characteristic specified in the above set
queue command.  The reason for defining the logical in the group table is
because it doesn't work if in the process table (it's supposed to, it just 
doesn't).  It will also work if defined/system.

Not exactly what you wanted, I know, but it will at least allow you to define
some basic default settings for your printer options.

Kelly

