The prefetching decision is made as soon as intructions are pulled
from the I-cache, while the actual branch target calculation happens
many cycles down the pipeline. On the first Alpha AXP chip, a successful
branch prediction saves 4 cycles (more if the target register is updated
just before the branching instruction).
