>Can one put a standard multisync RGB monitor on a Vaxstation 4000/60
>and make it work, or do i have to use a VRTnn type monitor from DEC??

Yes - the latest NEC MultiSync monitors support most DEC graphics standards,
notably 1024 x 1280 x 66Hz and 1024 x 1280 x 72Hz which are the relevant ones
for the VS4060. The NEC will pick up sync "where ever it finds it", so you can
just plug'n'play.

>In the same breath can I make a VRT16 DEC monitor work on a PC clone?

Yes (always supposing your PC card is 1024 x 1280), but it depends on which
VRT16 version you have. Some VRT16s only have 66Hz, others have 66Hz and 72Hz.
Another problem is that the VRT16 expects the sync to come on the G line. That
may not be compatible with your PC graphics card. Try it! I don't think you can
break anything (BUT I DON'T ACCEPT RESPONSIBILITY FOR ANY ACCIDENTS!!!!)

>I don't seem to be getting a straight answer from the DEC support people!

Funny that...

