reserved for MS-DOS.  All of them that are defined in the version of
MS-DOS you're running will work on the Rainbow.

> The IBM PC crowd tend to believe that _all_ of the INTs supported on that
> platform are MS-DOS interrupts, so they call them freely.

This can be a real problem with porting code between the PC and the
Rainbow.  Code Blue does however do a decent job of emulating the PC
BIOS on the Rainbow;  most things that use just the BIOS interface
will work properly on the Rainbow with Code Blue.  The major exceptions
are programs that are very timing dependent (very rare), and programs
that go directly to the hardware (this includes graphics, since the PC
BIOS graphics support is so rotten that virtually nothing uses it
exclusively, relying instead on direct hardware writes to achieve
reasonable speed and functionality).

Bruce C. Wright


