In article <C29quL.9qo@news.cso.uiuc.edu>, schwartz@feh.scs.uiuc.edu (Dwight A. Schwartz) writes:
> 
> Second, I'm looking for documentation on MS-DOS v. 2.11 interrupts and
> how to call them.  Can I assume that most/all of the interrupts in DOS for
> the Rainbow are the same as those for PC-DOS (the docs for which I think I
> can easily track down)?

Well, yes, as long as we're careful to separate the MS-DOS interrupts from
the IBM PC ROM BIOS interrupts. Basically, INT 21 works the same, but 
other INTs are _not_ MS-DOS interrupts and will behave differently on the
the Rainbow.

The IBM PC crowd tend to believe that _all_ of the INTs supported on that
platform are MS-DOS interrupts, so they call them freely.
