	The problem with N-ported SCSI is it doesn't tend to address these
kinds of things right. You can hang your bus at the drop of a hat. So, if
you're using multihosted SCSI to try to provide some kind of improved
reliability, now you can't hot-swap dead disks without crashing all your
systems. Ugh. Maybe someone should publish a paper about "Why SCSI is
