Sure. Your local Radio Shack.  We had the same problem here just last week
with our VS3100.  Had to put the kbrd, mouse and (mono VR-260) monitor in an 
adjacent room.  The biggest problem was getting a 5/8" 20" masonry bit (and a 
drill hefty enough to run it) to blast a hole through a structural wall of the 
ancient building which houses our lab.  Once that was over it was all downhill:

1. Get some RG-58/U coax cable and male BNCs to make your video extension
   cable.  Make three of 'em for color.  Ours is ~50 feet long and does
   not degrade the VR-260's image.

2. The DEC keyboard uses regular four conductor phone line.  Cut your 
   monitor cable in two and splice in a 50' extension.  Be sure to use 
   shrink tubing around each solder connection.  A 5" section of larger 
   shrink tubing around all the splices gives an even snazzier look.

3. Chop ypur mouse cable in two; check out the number of conductors
   (shielding counts!), buy 50' of appropriate cable, and proceed as above.

In steps 2 and 3 you may want to install male and female mini-connectors
to make your extension cables removable.

Be sure to power down your machine before removing any cables and reconnect
all before powering up.

Enjoy!

