In article <2B71B8A7.6782@news.service.uci.edu>, fredv@abba.acs.uci.edu (Fred Velijanian) writes:
|> Does anyone use FDDI with VAXstation 4000 Model 60s? The Nov 1992
|> System & Options Catalog lists the DEFZA-AA as an option for
|> VAXstation 4000/90, but not for 4000/60. (You first need to have
|> the DWCTX-BX TURBOchannel Adapter Module.)
|> 
|> Also anyone using LAVC over these FDDI controllers? We are 
|> investigating increasing LAVC performance using FDDI between
|> a few VAXstations and AXPs.
|> 

We are currently running VS4000/90s with the Turbo/FDDI option as members
of MI VAXclusters in more than one location.  I don't think it's available for
the /60 tho.

For a VAXcluster interface it works fine, but you can't boot off of the FDDI
interface (ie, no FxA0 device to say "BOOT FXA0").  We have gotten around
this by continuing to have both the Ethernet *and* the FDDI network connections
on the /90s.  It turns out that SCS listens on the wire(s) to determine the
path of least resistance (so to speak), and will use the one that is best.  In our
case this turns out to be the FDDI path most of the time.

The gotchas are that you must be sure that DECnet, LAT, (others?) use the
FDDI interface *or* the Ethernet interface - depending on how you want to
do things.  DECnet and LAT can *NOT* use BOTH interfaces because they
both use the DECnet address as their e-net physical address, and it ain't
kosher to have to devices with the same address on the same LAN (really
confuses the hell out of bridges too).

Also, be aware that there is currently a bug in the Pathworks/MAC client
(and probably AlisaShare too since it's Apple's bug) that will not allow the
LAT TOOL to work well for terminal emulation sessions.  For example, my versaterm
pro is setup to use the LAT TOOL, and my systems (VAX 6000s) have LAT on the
FDDI interface.  I connect to the system, login, etc., and everything looks find.....
until I fire-up a screen-oriented application (like an EDITOR).  Then the process
just dies.

I think DEC has taken the lead here to fix this for Apple, but I haven't seen it
just yet (tho that does not mean it's not available yet).

Hope this helps.
