I recently bought two Prestoserve boards for use on a 5000/240 and 5000/200
running Ultrix 4.3.  The one on the 240 works fine; I've found to my chagrin,
however, that Presto is incompatible with my 200.  When you do a "cnfg 5" at the
monitor prompt, you get -- among other things -- a statement
	PMAZ-AA		DEC	5.3b
The Turbochannel needs to be up to a Rev 5.3s or above to be able to recognize
the Presto board for what it is (on a 200; I think any 240 works).  If you,
like me, have an older unit, the FCO needed to upgrade will cost in excess of
$6000, which is rather more than you might have thought when pricing Presto
in the first place!  The available sales literature, BTW, fails to mention
such details.  I imagine the same caveats will apply to other "older" machines
on which one might want to use Presto.  

