No, VMS has never been ported to to MIPS; the machine does not support the facilities
required for VMS.  Look at the CACM article this month on what was required to
port VMS to Alpha for the reasons why this wasn't feasible.  PALcode on Alpha is used
to implement the facilities VMS requires without complicating the basic Alpha architecture.
These include 4 protection modes, AST support, interlocked queue support, etc.
