There are very few cases where you have to give VEST hints for it 
to get a translation right.  Self modifying code isn't one of them.  
The only case I can think of off the top of my head is when you're 
doing something like:

	CALLS	#0, foo
bar:	
		.
		.
		.

	MOVL	return_pc(FP), R0
	CMPL	R0, #bar


so what you have is code that does a CALL and then code that later checks
the return PC of the call instruction to see who called it. 

There may be a couple others but they're few and far between.  We've had
many 'naive' users use VEST to migrate their software without having
to do much of anything to get it to work.  And we use VEST ourselves to 
produce VEST running on OpenVMS AXP and don't have to manually provide
hints to get it to translate correctly.

