I'm not sure why you are having trouble doing this with Kermit, but here is
another option...

   Get a copy of UUTool or UULite for the mac, and UUENCODE/UUDECODE for VMS.
   You can then uuencode them on your VAX, then uudecode them on you mac after
   sending them with Kermit.  You can also do the reverse.  GNU Compress (or
   another unix-compatible compression program) for VMS and maccompress are
   also nice to have around if you plan to send things other than GIF files
   (they are already compressed).

   UUTool, UULite, and maccompress are available via anonymous ftp from
   sumex-aim.stanford.edu.  UUENCODE/UUDECODE for VMS and a unix-compatible
   compression program are available via anonymous ftp from ftp.spc.edu.

-Bill

