MAJOR SOFTWARE COMPANIES TO EXHIBIT AT DECUS '93/ATLANTA

Cognos, Ross Systems, SmartStar, SAS and WordPerfect To
Join Over 85 Other Companies At New DECUS Trade Show June 8-10


SHREWSBURY, Mass., January, 29, 1993 --  The Digital Equipment Computer 
Users Society (DECUS) today announced five major software companies will 
join the prominent list of companies exhibiting at DECUS '93/Atlanta, a 
one-week event featuring a new trade show, 100 seminars and 1,000 
sessions.  The sessions and seminars run June 5-11 and the trade show runs 
June 8-10.

Cognos, Inc., Ross Systems, Inc., SAS Institute Inc., SmartStar Corp. and
WordPerfect Corp. will exhibit at the new event.  They join a list of more 
than 85 additional vendors that will also be exhibiting at DECUS 
'93/Atlanta at The Georgia World Congress Center.  Over 70 percent of 
targeted exhibition space has already been booked, according to DECUS 
trade show officials.  

According to newly committed exhibitor SmartStar Corporation, based in 
Goleta, Calif., the new DECUS event offers many benefits.

"SmartStar decided to exhibit at DECUS '93/Atlanta this year primarily 
because the new trade show is located right with the technical symposium 
and seminars, making it very convenient for attendees and a more direct 
tie-in to the heart and soul of DECUS," said Tom Reyburn, marketing 
specialist at SmartStar Corp.  "Where else can you go, and under one roof, 
learn about the product technically, then walk down the hall and see a
demonstration of it and get the information you need to make a buying 
decision?  It's all here at one place, at one time."

Although DECUS has conducted national symposia and seminars for the past 
30 years, DECUS '93/Atlanta marks the first time DECUS will include a 
trade show in its mix of offerings.  The trade show will become a regular 
part of all future DECUS national events. 

"We are delighted these prominent software companies will exhibit at our 
first trade show in Atlanta this June," said Margaret Knox, president of 
the U.S. Chapter of DECUS.  "We've been pleased with the positive response 
from both attendees and vendors about this new addition to the event.  We 
believe interest is so strong because DECUS is made up of a real world mix 
of multiplatform users. 

"The 52,000 -plus people who make up DECUS in the U.S. are on the cutting 
edge of technology implementations, using products from Digital, Apple, 
HP, Sun and IBM as well as desktop solutions from vendors such as 
Microsoft and a wide variety of software.  This open computing reality is 
the focus of this and future DECUS events.  We look forward to a very 
successful trade show debut."

In June 1992, DECUS announced it would create its own trade show held at 
the same time and place as its national seminars and symposia.  This 
three-tiered event will now become a semiannual occurrence.  A 
distinguishing element of DECUS '93/Atlanta is the more than 1,000 
technology sessions, which cover a range of industry wide, multiplatform 
topics.

To receive a copy of the DECUS '93/Atlanta Information Packet (available 
in late March) contact DECUS Customer Service at 508-841-3914. Or send 
your request along with your name and full mailing address via the 
Internet to: information @decus.org.

The U.S. Chapter of DECUS promotes the exchange of information among 
people interested in Digital-related and open platform products, services 
and technologies. It is dedicated to advancing user interests and making 
their organizations more successful. There are over 120,000 members 
worldwide, including 52,000 members in the U.S. Chapter. 

DECUS members solve their organizations' computing problems and stay 
informed about industry issues and emerging technologies with the aid of 
