If you have access to the rzdisk utility on a DECstation, you can use that to set the disk to
spin up on powerup.   The syntax, I believe, is like this :

rzdisk -c ask /dev/rz??

where rz?? is the name of the raw device. You have to be super user to do this.   It will step
through a list of settable parameters, including the spin-up-on-power bit.  Once set, the
bit stays set until re-set.

Good luck.

