(Tom F Karlsson) writes:
> In article <31JAN199323335158@dt3> 9999sc01@dt3 (Alexandre Khalil) writes:
> 
>>    I have this RGB DEC monitor marked VR-241
>>    - Is it of any use? Can I recycle it for use with another computer ?
> 
> It's a very good color-monitor with quite high resolution. I use VR-241s
> on my Professional and Rainbow machines, but you can use it with almost
> any other computer with RGB output...

Actually, no, you can't.  It's limited to RS170 timing, ie 60 Hz vertical,
15750 Hz horizontal.  It does not do multi-sync.  

You can use it on any computer that has RGB output, with sync either on green
or on a separate line (a single line with both H and V sync), with suitable
timing.  In particular, it WON'T work on EGA, VGA, XGA, etc.  I think you could
connect it to a CGA card (the timing is right, but I don't know if CGA cards
used RGB outputs), but why bother?  

It seems to me that the early Amigas and Atari ST's used RGB with RS170 timing,
but I think they too have moved on to better things.  

Sell it to someone with a VT240, GIGI, or Rainbow or Pro-3x0 with a graphics
card, who has a b&w monitor and wants to move up to color. 

